.TH HMAP_ADD_TUPLE_WITH_DATA 3 "15 Mar 2023" "CB" "Library Functions"

.SH NAME
hmap_add_tuple_with_data \- Add a tuple with associated data to a hash map

.SH SYNOPSIS
.IB #include <lib/hmap_internal.h>

.IB int
.IB hmap_add_tuple_with_data(HMAP_DB** hmap_db, const void* key, size_t k_len, void* data);

.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBhmap_add_tuple_with_data\fR function adds a tuple with associated data to a hash map. It takes a pointer to the hash map database, the key, the length of the key, and the data as arguments.

The function takes the following parameters:
.IB HMAP_DB**
A pointer to the hash map database.
.IB const void*
The key to be added to the hash map.
.IB size_t
The length of the key.
.IB void*
The data to be associated with the key.

The function returns an integer indicating the result of the operation. Possible return values include:
.IB HMAP_SUCCESS
The tuple was added successfully.
.IB HMAP_TUPLE_ALREADY_EXIST
The tuple already exists in the hash map.
.IB HMAP_TUPLE_NOT_FOUND
The tuple was not found in the hash map.
.IB HMAP_ALLOCATED_ERROR
An error occurred during memory allocation.

The \fBhmap_add_tuple_with_data\fR function is intended to be used to add tuples with associated data to a hash map.

.SH EXAMPLES
The following example demonstrates how to use the \fBhmap_add_tuple_with_data\fR function to add a tuple with associated data to a hash map:

.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <lib/hmap_internal.h>

int main() {
    HMAP_DB* hmap_db;
    // Initialize the hash map database
    hmap_init(&hmap_db);

    // Add a tuple with associated data
    int result = hmap_add_tuple_with_data(&hmap_db, "example", 7, "data");

    if(result == HMAP_SUCCESS) {
        printf("Tuple added successfully\n");
    } else {
        printf("Failed to add tuple\n");
    }

    // Free the hash map database
    hmap_free(&hmap_db);

    return 0;
}
.nef